# ============================================================
# WebHawk (Python / Flask) - .gitignore
# Development happens on native Windows, in VS Code and PyCharm.
# Both editors' project folders are ignored, since they hold
# machine-specific paths (interpreter location, run configs) that
# would conflict between machines if committed.
# ============================================================

# --- Secrets ---
# Real credentials live only here. .env.example is the committed template.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# --- Python bytecode / build artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# --- Virtual environments ---
# Windows convention is usually .venv\ or venv\ at the repo root.
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Testing / coverage ---
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/

# --- VS Code ---
# Everything ignored except settings/extensions that are genuinely shared
# (the "!" lines re-include them). Same approach the C++ repo uses for
# .vscode/c_cpp_properties.json.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json

# --- PyCharm / JetBrains ---
# .idea/ holds the absolute path to each person's Python interpreter and
# their local run configurations - never portable between machines.
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# --- Windows OS junk ---
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
# Created by Windows when a file is downloaded from the internet (e.g. a
# zip pulled from the browser). Harmless, but noisy in `git status`.
*Zone.Identifier*

# --- macOS / Linux (teammates may not all be on Windows) ---
.DS_Store
*~

# --- Logs ---
*.log
logs/